WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.300
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, my Bonus Video
this week will be all about Braavos.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.000
The episode 6 teaser had a bunch of scenes
at the Iron Bank, so I thought this would

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.370
be the perfect time to talk about it.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.850
We’re really just seeing the city for the
first time so what I’m going to do is talk

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.440
a little bit about where it is in relation
to Meereen and Slaver’s Bay, what the big

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.689
groups are and the Iron Bank’s role on the
show.

00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:24.699
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do bonus videos for Game of Thrones every

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:26.800
week in addition to reviews of the episodes
and Q&amp;As.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.609
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
feel free to leave me suggestions for videos

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:31.609
to do.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:33.040
So first order of business.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.719
Because some of you may have read the books,
please try to be careful about posting spoilers

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:39.539
in the comments, or at least use spoiler tags.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.800
We’re not really sure how much the show
is going to change about what goes on in Braavos,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.800
so best to play it safe.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.460
Whenever I post my review I’ll talk about
what those big changes are.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.850
So WTF is Braavos?

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.410
If you saw the trailers, then this image here.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:54.620
It’s the Titan of Braavos.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.550
It’s one of the 9 wonders of man.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.789
It’s inspired by the Colossus of Rhodes
for any history buffs.

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:03.949
But the Titan is the most visible symbol of
the city.

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:06.650
It’s even stamped on Braavosi coins.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.840
And passing beneath the Titan is the only
way for ships to enter the port.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.630
Braavos itself is the most powerful of the
Free Cities.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:20.170
It’s located in a lagoon way up North on
the tip of the eastern continent.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:25.170
The city itself exists on a series of small
islands connected by bridges.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.450
Remember how Daenerys is in Meereen right
now?

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.890
She’s way down here on the other side of
the continent.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:35.020
The city formed about 500 years before Aegon’s
Landing in Westeros from people fleeing the

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.070
Valyrian Expansion.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.560
It’s nicknamed the Bastard Son of Valyria
because the people that colonized it were

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.700
trying to hide from Valyria’s dragons.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.700
So it wasn’t till after the doom that Braavos
started to make itself known to the rest of

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.700
the world.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.189
It’s a port city that draws it’s wealth
from trade and shipping, and as a result it’s

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:52.110
one of the wealthiest cities in the world.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.810
Thus the Iron Bank of Braavos became the most
powerful bank in the world.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:02.390
The most notable locations in the city are
the Titan itself, Drowned Town which is an

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.320
area where the city has sunken into the lagoon,
The House of Black and White which is the

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.700
Temple of the Many Faced God, there are temples
to a lot of different gods that all exist

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.290
in an area called the isle of the gods.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:20.330
So as you see the temple of R’hollor Melisandre’s
god is here too, there’s Purple Harbor which

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.750
is really only used by locals near the Sealord’s
palace.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.310
He’s the ruler of Braavos.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.360
Then there’s the Iron Bank here.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.740
This is where the scene with Mark Gatiss in
the trailer takes place.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.920
There’s Ragman’s Harbor, which is used
by most foreign traders visiting on business

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:45.010
and then the Temple of the Moonsingers, they
were actually the people that found the site

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.319
where Braavos would eventually be located
after they fled Valyria.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:55.600
There’s a billion different locations so
the next time the show comes here I’ll go

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.420
into greater detail about the different locations.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.150
The most important location for right now
is the Iron Bank.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:06.050
It’s the one common denominator amongst
all the factions on the show.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:09.880
You can’t win the Iron Throne without a
war or a marriage.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.210
And both cost money.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.800
Which as we learned from Tywin Lannister last
week, no one has.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.840
The Tyrells are wealthy, but most of their
assets are in farmland.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.610
So the only way to get more money is to borrow
it from the Iron Bank.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:29.709
Just to give you an idea of how powerful it
is, it’s bigger than all the other banks

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.709
in the free cities combined.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:31.709
It’s the biggest bank in the world.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:34.280
It’s mostly known for the way it goes after
debts.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.980
Which is funny, because up to this point on
the show we’ve heard the Lannister motto

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:38.980
so many times.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.319
A Lannister always pays his debts.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:48.740
The Iron Bank’s motto is “The Iron Bank
will have it’s due”.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.670
What happens when a King or a nation borrows
money and doesn’t pay them back is the Iron

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.610
Bank will support a new King.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:07.150
And 

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:12.349
once they install said new King, that person
has to repay the original debt or the Iron

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:16.630
Bank will do the exact same thing and replace
them with another King.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:21.419
So when you think about it, the Iron Bank
is the most powerful organization in the World.

00:04:21.419 --> 00:04:23.360
Even the Iron Throne has to bow to them.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.370
Which is why Stannis in the trailer almost
looks like he’s begging Mark Gatiss for

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:28.370
money.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.169
The conceit being that because King Robert
borrowed so much money and never paid it back,

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:34.889
Stannis will probably try to convince them
to back his claim in exchange for repayment

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:35.889
of the debt.

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:39.379
I don’t know how the show is going to deal
with that plot, but I’m interested to see

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:42.279
what terms they set for Stannis.

00:04:42.279 --> 00:04:46.349
And remember, if Stannis does get a loan and
doesn’t pay it back.

00:04:46.349 --> 00:04:51.129
The Iron Bank could always turn around and
fund one of his enemies.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:54.930
Needless to say, the Iron Bank controls the
flow of money and therefore it controls the

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:55.979
balance of war.

00:04:55.979 --> 00:05:01.419
Based on the teaser for episode 6 it’s hard
to tell which other places we might get to

00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:06.580
see, but her in the harbor you can see the
Sealord’s palace.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:12.089
But we might get to see some waterdancers
or maybe a few easter eggs.

00:05:12.089 --> 00:05:15.860
Remember how Arya was practicing her waterdancing
for the Hound last week.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.409
Syrio Forel who taught her was one of the
Bravos.

00:05:19.409 --> 00:05:23.360
Just one O in bravos.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.099
They’re a special class of fighters that
developed the waterdancing technique and they

00:05:29.099 --> 00:05:33.499
dress in really bright loud colors as you
can see.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.770
The wealthy people in the city all dress in
really drab grey colors.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:44.870
As you can see Mark Gatiss, wealthy banker
here.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:48.680
Anyone in Braavos carrying a sword after dark
can be challenged to a duel, it doesn’t

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:49.680
matter who you are.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.910
It’s just part of the culture that they
challenge each other constantly just for bragging

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.029
rights as the best fighter in the city.

00:05:56.029 --> 00:06:00.389
So say someone like Syrio Forel probably had
to fight people every single night.

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:04.669
And because he lived to a pretty decent age
it meant he was a badass.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:10.249
The place where most of them go to duel is
the Moon Pool here, right near the Iron Bank.

00:06:10.249 --> 00:06:14.770
So there’s a good chance we’ll see it
in episode 6.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:22.630
The city also has a really strong tradition
of Courtesans that hold a special status in

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.999
the culture.

00:06:23.999 --> 00:06:25.810
They command extremely high prices.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:29.770
So just think of the money a prince with Oberyn
Martell’s appetites would spend.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.050
Like a kid in a candy store.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:35.139
All the best whore houses are either up here
in the Purple Harbor.

00:06:35.139 --> 00:06:36.419
Or around the Moon Pool.

00:06:36.419 --> 00:06:39.830
Isn’t it funny that all the best sex in
the city is right next to the bank.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.430
I guess that says something about people’s
priorities.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:43.430
Sex and Money.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:44.430
Seems about right.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.639
I’m really hoping that we get to see more
of the city this season just because it’s

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:49.379
so much fun to talk about.

00:06:49.379 --> 00:06:54.310
Of all the cities that the show has depicted,
I would say this is the best, with Meereen

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.069
being number 2, even though we haven’t seen
a lot of it yet.

00:06:57.069 --> 00:06:58.710
And King’s Landing third.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.460
Unless you count the Lands of Always Winter
we saw in episode 4.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.839
That white walker city looked pretty sweet.

00:07:04.839 --> 00:07:09.050
But now it’s your turn, what are you hoping
to see in Braavos this week?

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:14.460
I know a lot of the Doctor Who and Sherlock
fans are excited to see Mark Gatiss.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.219
Given what we know about his character from
the books, I’m really interested to see

00:07:17.219 --> 00:07:21.449
if he plays it more like Mycroft or if he’s
going to play it a little lighter.

00:07:21.449 --> 00:07:26.059
He essentially has the task of showing us
what that motto means, The Iron Bank Will

00:07:26.059 --> 00:07:27.059
Have It’s Due.

00:07:27.059 --> 00:07:30.409
So I’m expecting a scarier version of Mycroft.

00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:33.830
I’ll be posting my episode 6 review tonight
after it airs.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:35.149
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:35.149 --> 00:07:36.149
Round 6 of the giveaway will also be starting
then.

